<title>USA: Mazel Stores Q1 shr $0.17 vs pro forma.</title>
<headline>Mazel Stores Q1 shr $0.17 vs pro forma.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>MAZEL STORES, INC.</p>
<p>			   COMBINED STATEMENT OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>			(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					  Apr 26, 1997     Apr 30, 1996</p>
<p> Net sales				$   43,128	 $   42,455</p>
<p> Gross profit				 14,844	     12,899</p>
<p>    % of sales				34.42%	     30.38%</p>
<p> SG&amp;A					   12,220		9,899</p>
<p> Operating profit			    2,624		3,000</p>
<p>    % of sales				 6.08%		7.07%</p>
<p> Interest (income) expense		    45		  591</p>
<p> Other (income) expense		    (107)		  (8)</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		2,686		2,417</p>
<p> Income taxes				  1,155		   79</p>
<p> Net income				    1,531		2,338</p>
<p> Net income per share			 0.17</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	  9,170,100</p>
<p>Pro Forma As Adjusted Data (1)</p>
<p> Sales								 42,455</p>
<p> Income before income taxes				     3,567</p>
<p> Income taxes							 1,427</p>
<p> Pro forma net income as adjusted			     2,140</p>
<p>Pro forma net income per share as adjusted</p>
<p>									   0.23</p>
<p>Average pro forma shares outstanding</p>
<p>								    9,170,100 (1)</p>
<p>Pro forma as adjusted data gives effect to the Company's initial public offering as of the beginning of all periods presented, and includes the combination of:  (i) the Mazel wholesale operations; (ii) the Odd Job retail operations; (iii) the Peddlers Mart retail store, as if the combination of entities had occurred at the beginning of all periods presented.  Pro forma as adjusted data exclude certain non-recurring charges, and give effect to the use of proceeds resulting from the Company's 2,960,100 share initial public offering, as well as certain adjustments to compensation expense.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
